lesson k-weather-words v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=9 subject=language levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "[[weather.it-is-sunny|cap]]"
  goal "Say the weather in [[language.name]]."

  look {
    scene 8x6 {
      cloud c puffs=4 rain=1 at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
        Weather in [[language.name]]: it is sunny is [[weather.it-is-sunny]], it is raining is
        [[weather.it-is-raining]], it is hot is [[weather.it-is-hot]] and it is cold is
        [[weather.it-is-cold]]. Look outside and say the weather each day.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.lang-weather-meaning k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.lang-weather-meaning count=3 seed=2 easy-count=2 hard-count=2
    show k.lang-weather-picture r=1 hard-r=0
    show k.lang-what-to-wear k=0 hard-k=1
    show k.lang-say-weather
    practice k.lang-food-meaning count=2 seed=9 easy-count=1
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.lang-hot-cold
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.lang-two-weathers k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "[[weather.it-is-sunny|cap]], [[weather.it-is-raining]], [[weather.it-is-hot]], [[weather.it-is-cold]]."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read every phrase aloud and let the child say it back; the child picks from what you read. The
    weather and the seasons named weather in English; this lesson is the step on from the food words,
    whole phrases of two words that describe the day rather than single words for things. The weather
    talk is for you to listen to over a week. Off the page, say the weather in the language when you
    open the curtains each morning. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 言葉, 内容 (7):
    "生活の中で言葉の楽しさや美しさに気付く。" (Notice the fun and beauty of words in daily life.) The
    phrases are in [[language.variety]].
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level sunny is worked in the teacher's pen first, the phrases are sunny and raining, and the coat goes with cold."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the phrases are hot and cold, the sun hat goes with hot, and the three-star is sunny and hot."
  }
}
